{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Young1967-caseF-thin-thick-39L",
  "Source": "L. Young, \"Multilayer Interference Filters with Narrow Stop Bands,\" Appl. Opt. 6, 297-315 (1967). doi:10.1364/AO.6.000297 - Sec. VII pp. 309-311: Eqs. (49)-(50), Table I currents (p. 305), y = 40; Figs. 14 and 15/16",
  "Notes": "Narrow stop-band filter of alternating thin high-index (ZnS) and thick low-index (MgF2) layers, thin-layer phase thicknesses proportional to 40-dB Dolph-Chebyshev currents (20 elements), y = 40\nSpecification: Stop band at theta/90 = 1 (reference_nm), equal-ripple-like passband; thin layers spaced 180 deg centre to centre.\nReported: Fig. 15 (plot only): peak attenuation about 28 dB (transmittance ~0.0016) at theta/90 = 1; ripples computed for theta/90 = 0.5-1.5 only, reflectance ripples between ~0.0005 and 0.002-0.01 rising linearly with frequency; the two centre thin layers are 40 deg thick, each alone giving SWR V = 1.96 (Eqs. 52-53, p. 312), i.e. R = 0.105 for a single 40-deg ZnS layer in MgF2. Second stop band at theta/90 = 2. Recomputed here: centre attenuation 28.06 dB.\nNotes: 39 layers (20 thin + 19 thick). Thin layers (odd i): theta_i = y*I_{(i+1)/2} deg with y = 40 and the 20-element Table I currents (symmetric); thick layers (even i): theta_i = 180 - (theta_{i-1} + theta_{i+1})/2 deg (Eq. 50). Thickness in QWOT = theta/90 at reference_nm (arbitrary 550 nm), rounded to 8 decimals. Phase thicknesses in degrees: 4.708, 174.334, 6.624, 171.416, 10.544, 167.104, 15.248, 162.142, 20.468, 156.85, 25.832, 151.636, 30.896, 146.948, 35.208, 143.224, 38.344, 140.828, 40, 140, 40, 140.828, 38.344, 143.224, 35.208, 146.948, 30.896, 151.636, 25.832, 156.85, 20.468, 162.142, 15.248, 167.104, 10.544, 171.416, 6.624, 174.334, 4.708. Paper: thick layers n1 = 1.38 or 2.3, thin layers n2 = 2.3 or 1.38 (\"only the ratio 0.6 figured\"); here thin = ZnS 2.3, thick and both end media = MgF2 1.38 (the stack is embedded in the thick-layer medium, Fig. 14). Normal incidence, lossless.\nLayers from Sec. VII pp. 309-311: Eqs. (49)-(50), Table I currents (p. 305), y = 40; Figs. 14 and 15/16; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours 28.06 dB at the centre; paper about 28 dB (Figs. 15-16).",
